[2026-10-28 21:25:47.003 IFO][NeuroDragon] [vvsr] sr mv: engine arg11=0x27a288142d0 fmt=10 layout=zw (1689x903, pixels current->previous)
[2026-10-28 21:25:47.004 IFO][NeuroDragon] [vvsr] sr arg10 #1800: 2560x1369 fmt=26 eval=1 mv=engine
[2026-10-28 21:25:47.019 IFO][NeuroDragon] [vv] inject: arg10 boundary split=48/70 list=0x27a07a80210 target=0x27a2880d9a0
# 9 skips total = 1 arm + 8 suppressed frames; the next frame injected normally.

## 5. Conclusions

# 1. Whole-callback suppress: arg10 is NOT bound as an RTV by any list (writer=0 on all
#    8 frames). The current writer anchor would disappear; a suppress that skips the
#    callback cannot reuse the arg10 writer cut.
# 2. arg11 has no declarator-side channel (dep2 holder is not a pointer); the MV role
#    channel exists only inside the draw's material binding. Suppressing the callback
#    also removes MV capture (mv value stays at the last forwarded frame).
# 3. The TAAU draw itself IS identifiable inside the arg10 writer list: first draw,
#    DrawIndexedInstanced(6,1), bind-time exact tag. => the viable suppress is
#    "skip only this draw call, keep the callback and its material bindings": the
#    writer anchor survives, MV keeps updating, and the TAAU draw leaves the submission.
